# Metal Forming World (MFW) mobile application
#
# This repository is public. This file keeps secrets, reader data, MFW's
# confidential files and generated output out of Git (CODING_STANDARDS.md
# section 13; DEC-012, DEC-024; SEC-CHK-09). It is a safety net: it hides
# files from `git status`, but it does not remove a file that is already
# tracked. Run the secrets scan (QG-11, once it exists) as well.
#
# The folders app/, backend/ and admin/ do not exist yet (DEC-012). Entries
# for tools whose choice is still open (DEC-003, DEC-004) are marked
# PROVISIONAL and are to be confirmed when that tooling is first run.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and credentials (CODING_STANDARDS.md section 13, item 1)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Android signing
*.jks
*.keystore
key.properties
**/key.properties

# Apple signing and push keys, provisioning profiles
*.p12
*.p8
*.mobileprovision
*.provisionprofile

# Service-account key files
*service-account*.json
*serviceAccount*.json
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
# PROVISIONAL (TD-03): local server configuration written by the platform tooling
.runtimeconfig.json

# Environment files with values. Only the example files are tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Configuration for each environment (DEPLOYMENT_PLAN.md section 5). Everything
# in config/ is ignored except the example, so a new file there is never
# committed by accident.
/config/*
!/config/config.example.env

# Provider mobile configuration files are not secrets, but they are specific
# to an environment. Whether they are committed is decided with DEC-003 and
# DEC-023 (CODING_STANDARDS.md section 13, item 3). Until then they stay out.
# PROVISIONAL: delete these two lines if that decision says to commit them.
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MFW files and reader data (DEC-024)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# MFW's sample PDFs are confidential, and no reader data may be committed.
# Where large fixtures and MFW samples are stored is not decided (DEC-024), so
# a PDF is ignored everywhere except in Documentation/, which already holds the
# proposal and the statement of work. When a fixtures folder is decided, add a
# negation for that folder's path in the same pull request. Fixtures are
# generated or public files, never MFW's samples.
*.pdf
!/Documentation/*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating system and editor files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/
.history/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and general output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

*.log
build/
dist/
coverage/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Flutter and Dart (app/). pubspec.lock is tracked (QG-10 reads it).
# `flutter create` also writes its own .gitignore inside app/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.dart_tool/
.pub-cache/
.pub/
.packages
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.gradle/
.cxx/
.kotlin/
**/android/local.properties
**/android/captures/
**/android/**/GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
**/ios/Pods/
**/ios/.symlinks/
**/ios/Flutter/ephemeral/
**/ios/Flutter/Generated.xcconfig
**/ios/Flutter/flutter_export_environment.sh
**/ios/Flutter/App.framework
**/ios/Flutter/Flutter.framework
**/ios/Flutter/flutter_assets/
**/ios/Runner/GeneratedPluginRegistrant.*
**/macos/Flutter/ephemeral/
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node.js and TypeScript (backend/ and admin/). The layouts are blocked by
# DEC-003 and DEC-004. package-lock.json is tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.npm/
.eslintcache
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local emulator output. PROVISIONAL (TD-03): confirm the file names when the
# emulators are first run, and add the folder that holds any exported
# emulator data once its name is chosen.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.firebase/
# *.log above already covers the emulator logs. This covers rotated copies.
*-debug.log.*
